'''Barrio Tekami''' ({{Literal translation|Tekami quarter}}) is a relatively densely populated residential neighborhood in the [[Arrayán]] borough of the city of [[Axarquía]], within [[Araucaria]].

Its name references the {{W|demographic shift|demographic transformation}} it underwent in the 1880s with the influx of immigrants from {{W|East Asia}}, most notably several hundred [[Sanese people|Sanese families]]. These new migrants quickly established themselves as the dominant economic demographic in the area, despite Sanese being a minority in the neighborhood. Their influence culminated in the development of the [[Barrio Tekami Community Plan]], by Okaiken-born and future delegate [[Koyasu Eikichi]], which envisioned the expansion of the community to 1,000 acres. For these reasons, the neighborhood came to be called Barrio Tekano. 

